    {
      "id": 107331353,
      "postUrl": "https://t.me/medmannews/47693?single",
      "source": {
        "title": "Mediterranean Man",
        "handle": "medmannews",
        "verified": false,
        "avatar": "https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/KUaP4RgjvcKdPeaSDcCCn2i5gSIFchlBJLBD1HTNvjs77x6HQLtuZqMAjclrgbS4ApvqYk64dK7DYSKuEqBcldov2EM7RvGaYyatpJjJM8hzxBdNLEVDD4R93WylbVz6t02zTSJ_0UGnVtujRya5XLWgBUHOp1qtDcRhpyAEESvfiaaguF_AJocUXf2gtsjIjllwwMiB3g1zEqh38mw0HkJcdHeUo9Ym-HZ0LZ2CDJxYLFC-Ri9h2E_3kcgAbOAeek0HqVsNHwQQvByXnCTklLEoIp-8EGzAQebAW2Hq5PUORYeayFQLtviOmxW8SSCL-w8eVn1zZufHqGjwi7qPVw.jpg"
      },
      "sourceId": "eg:medmannews",
      "sourceCountryCode": "eg",
      "contentType": "text",
      "media": [],
      "hasMediaInOriginal": false,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "But ah, some of you would die if I did not relate a story or two, and why should I be a cruel man and deprive you of this and that?\n\nBeing sent back reminded me that some people can be really, really desperate, in fact, their desperation might make them seem malicious, and while you have to be understanding of their condition you also have to understand that beyond a point there is nothing but a stick.\n\nI managed to buy myself a can of tuna because the Ugandan army is slightly better fed than me, it is hard to substitute on decayed dates and bread, watery meat, and suspicious rice, it was then when I opened the can did a cat (at this point, I did not see an animal for over three weeks) presented itself next to me, meowing for anything, on which with my spoon I gave it a spoonful of tuna, oil and the shredded tuna and all.\n\nA conscript then passed by, and with disgust in his voice told me with no irony that I was a moron for giving a cat a spoonful of tuna when the rest of them were starving.\n\nAt first I was understanding if I had given it half the can or the likes, but it was only a spoonful, then I realized that I actually outranked him by seniority, so I forced him to do pushups until failure and and made him what we call a \"Grill\", that is, we make him roll on the sand until I got bored and brought him up.\n\nNone of you from civilized countries would have imagined a man being so upset over a spoonful of a tuna can, but in certain conditions not only would that viewpoint be common, but also marginally acceptable, so try not to judge people so quickly, at least know what brought them so low before you do what you have to do.",
      "links": [],
      "createdAt": "2026-11-16T22:36:05.774Z",
      "expiresAt": "2026-11-18T22:36:05.774Z",
